                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Voltages can be both negative and zero.  If you're seeing negative values it likely means that your ADC ranging configuration is incorrect."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This appears to be a bad platform config that's trying to be covered up in a hacked patch.  If you don't want to see negative values on voltage sensors, make sure MinValue is set to 0.0"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/psu/PSUSensor.cpp",
                    "line": 239,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Voltage readings can be negative though.  How do we know when this is perhaps appropriate and when it is not?"
                }
            ],
